{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00953",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.7,
      "end_seconds": 15.32,
      "duration_seconds": 13.62,
      "text": "Good to see you again, Dana. It's about three weeks since we last spoke. How have things been since the accident? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 18.1,
      "end_seconds": 29.79,
      "duration_seconds": 11.69,
      "text": "Okay. Not great. I keep having these, I guess flashbacks? I see the truck, the lights, I'm back on the road."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.27,
      "end_seconds": 34.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "How often?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 37.01,
      "end_seconds": 48.83,
      "duration_seconds": 11.82,
      "text": "A couple of times a week. It started... I don't know. A month after? Maybe two? I can't really say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 51.45,
      "end_seconds": 53.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "And at night?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.54,
      "end_seconds": 63.4,
      "duration_seconds": 7.86,
      "text": "Nightmares. Bad ones. I wake up sweating, and I'm scared to go back to sleep."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 66.51,
      "end_seconds": 70.83,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "Have you had any thoughts of harming yourself?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.47,
      "end_seconds": 77.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "No. No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.1,
      "end_seconds": 85.59,
      "duration_seconds": 5.49,
      "text": "Are you drinking more than you used to?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.38,
      "end_seconds": 93.97,
      "duration_seconds": 5.59,
      "text": "No, not really. A glass of wine, same as always."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.19,
      "end_seconds": 100.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "Let's go through your medications."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.91,
      "end_seconds": 114.56,
      "duration_seconds": 10.65,
      "text": "Sertraline, 50 mg, once a day. Prazosin, 1 mg, at night, for the nightmares. And ibuprofen, 400 mg, when my leg aches."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.82,
      "end_seconds": 121.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "Do you take the sertraline every day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.42,
      "end_seconds": 130.3,
      "duration_seconds": 6.88,
      "text": "Every day. Well, most days. I forget it if I'm in a rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.23,
      "end_seconds": 138.12,
      "duration_seconds": 5.89,
      "text": "Okay. Thanks for being straight with me. Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 139.99,
      "end_seconds": 141.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "Penicillin. Hives."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.16,
      "end_seconds": 147.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Any other health problems?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 150.62,
      "end_seconds": 153.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "Anxiety, I guess. Before all this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.98,
      "end_seconds": 162.81,
      "duration_seconds": 6.83,
      "text": "And the accident, you had surgery on the leg, I believe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.58,
      "end_seconds": 171.82,
      "duration_seconds": 6.24,
      "text": "Yeah. A rod put in my left shin, four months ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.62,
      "end_seconds": 177.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "How's the leg? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 179.19,
      "end_seconds": 184.62,
      "duration_seconds": 5.43,
      "text": "Better. Sore if I walk a long way. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.83,
      "end_seconds": 203.04,
      "duration_seconds": 8.21,
      "text": "Let me look at you, Dana. You seem restless, shifting a lot in the chair."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.97,
      "end_seconds": 208.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "Yeah. I can't sit still. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.25,
      "end_seconds": 217.17,
      "duration_seconds": 4.92,
      "text": "Any chest pain or palpitations between the flashbacks?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 220.0,
      "end_seconds": 224.28,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "No, nothing, I'm fine between them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.12,
      "end_seconds": 236.99,
      "duration_seconds": 9.87,
      "text": "That's helpful. What you're describing, the flashbacks, the nightmares and the jumpiness, fits post-traumatic stress after the accident."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 238.9,
      "end_seconds": 241.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "PTSD? Like soldiers? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.28,
      "end_seconds": 252.25,
      "duration_seconds": 7.97,
      "text": "It's not just soldiers. Anyone who has been through something frightening can have it. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 254.57,
      "end_seconds": 258.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "Is it going to go away? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.92,
      "end_seconds": 269.34,
      "duration_seconds": 8.42,
      "text": "For most people, yes, with treatment. Keep taking your sertraline every day. It works best taken regularly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 271.81,
      "end_seconds": 275.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "I'll set an alarm. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.18,
      "end_seconds": 285.11,
      "duration_seconds": 6.93,
      "text": "Good idea. I'd like to see you again in two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 288.23,
      "end_seconds": 291.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "Two weeks. Okay. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.0,
      "end_seconds": 300.34,
      "duration_seconds": 7.34,
      "text": "And if it gets worse before then, ring the clinic. Don't wait. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 303.91,
      "end_seconds": 306.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "I will. ~"
    }
  ]
}
